    <briefdescription>
<para>Concept satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a string, convertible to a <computeroutput>std::basic_string_view</computeroutput> of a character type. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>string_like</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> object of type <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is implicitly convertible to a <computeroutput>std::basic_string_view</computeroutput> of <computeroutput>char</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>wchar_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char8_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char16_t</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>char32_t</computeroutput>, as the standard strings and the string views are. It is used to detect the strings, which the formatter writes as text, not element by element (see <computeroutput>formattable_range</computeroutput>). A container that has only a member named <computeroutput>npos</computeroutput>, or that is not convertible, is not a string. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
